-- title:
--   Level automorphisms: stabilising Wₜ iff fixing the chart point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$.
--
--   **Supersingular places and constant reduction.** $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ — the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ generated over the residue field of $A$ by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ composed with $q \mapsto q^{M'}$ — and `hW` requires $W$ to be exactly $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$, the set of places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hle` asks that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,j$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M'$, be contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former, a surjective residue map onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map on places compatible with the order functions, and compatibility with $A$ both on membership and on residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with termwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$, i.e. a chosen supersingular place.
--
--   **Constants group.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has its image in $A$; write $A_0$ for the valuation subring $A.\mathrm{comap}$ of $k_0$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` requires every element of $A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and uniformisers.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has its image in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. The bottom-field bookkeeping group consists of an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ required to equal $\bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Tame auxiliary prime and the function field.** $\ell'$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell'$, $\ell' \ne q$, $\ell' \nmid M'$, with $\ell'(\ell'^2-1)$ a unit in $A_0$ (`htame`), and $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity. $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ over $k_0$, required by `hKℓ` to be the $k_0$-base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$, where $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$. It carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $A_0 \to k_0 \to K_\ell$, and $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is a nonzero element whose underlying Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Moreover $\varpi_t'$ is an element of $A_0$ mapping to $\varpi_t$.
--
--   **The chart point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, such that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $y$ (`hϖy`), and such that (`hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$. The hypothesis `hover` says that $y$ lies over $s$: for every $g$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which is regular wherever $j$ is (at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, non-negativity of the order of $j$ implies non-negativity of the order of $g$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every witness that the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\ell'(g)$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, and every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that chart element and the image of $c$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states that any maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same lying-over condition (the clause of `hover` repeated verbatim with $y'$) is carried to $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,H\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ such that $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself and $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y'$ for chart elements. Here $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}$ expresses that $\tau$ realises the $\gamma^{-1}$-translation of modular functions: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $g$'s series nonzero, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the ratio of those two series, and every embedding $\iota$ of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   **The model and the exceptional valuation (`hS1`).** $B_t$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $W_t$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The conjunction `hS1` (summarised here clause by clause) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; the quotient of $B_t$ by the ideal generated by $\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; an element of $k_0$ lies in $W_t$ exactly when it comes from $A_0$; the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is generated by $\pi_0$ and $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ to the chart algebra; $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A_0$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,k$, the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,k - 1$, whose vanishing locus is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is compatible with $A_0 \to k$, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ in the above sense which preserves $W_t$ there is a unit $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the kernel of the character $(\bar\gamma,c) \mapsto \det(\bar\gamma)\,c^{q+1}$, such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}\,q\,k\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c) \circ \rho$ on $B_t$, such that $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity, and — the linked scalar clause — such that the same scalar $c$ is realised by a pair $(1,c)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ through some $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with an attached $\tau'$ preserving $W_t$; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ receives the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ under some level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ sent into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by every such level automorphism is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **The cyclic generator and the ends (`hR7`).** $n \ge 1$ divides $q+1$; $\gamma_0$ lies in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$; $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma_0^{-1}$ with $f \in W_t \iff \tau_0 f \in W_t$. Further, $m \ge 1$ satisfies $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'\,w$ for a unit $w$ of $A_0$; $\zeta_c$ is an element of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$; and `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K_\ell$. The conjunction `hR7` (summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0 < k < n$; every level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements; level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ permute `ends`, transitively; $\tau_0$ preserves each end; distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is a Noetherian local ring containing the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has every element congruent to an element of $A_0$ modulo non-units, and has adic completion $A_0$-isomorphic to the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at $\pi_0^m$, namely the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by $X_0X_1 - \pi_0^m$, by an isomorphism $\iota$ carrying suitable $c_x, c_y \in O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m$ times a unit to unit multiples of `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V`, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, and conjugating $\tau_0$ into an automorphism $\theta_0$ of the crossing model acting on those two elements by $\zeta_c$ and its inverse $\zeta_c'$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end moreover carries a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ containing $O$ and the chart algebra, meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, discrete with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, admitting an element transcendental in the residual sense recorded there, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, and whose contraction to the chart algebra is contained in $y$ but not equal to it; and a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $B_t \cap O$, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, whose elements are regular at every place of $K_\ell/k_0$ at which $j_\ell$ is, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its non-units. The final clause of `hR7` is a valuative dichotomy: every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, containing the chart algebra and with $y$ inside its maximal ideal, either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   **The uniqueness hypothesis (`hR5d`).** For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$: if $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y$ for all chart elements $b$ with $\tau b$ again in the chart algebra, then $f \in W_t \iff \tau f \in W_t$ for all $f \in K_\ell$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ such that there exists $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, the following two conditions are equivalent: (i) $f \in W_t \iff \tau f \in W_t$ for every $f \in K_\ell$; (ii) for every $b$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ and every witness that $\tau b$ again lies in that chart algebra, $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y$.
--
--   This is the dictionary identifying, for level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, the stabiliser of the exceptional valuation $W_t$ of the regular model of $X_H$ at a supersingular point with the stabiliser of the corresponding maximal ideal $y$ of the finite chart algebra. It feeds the computation of the order of the decomposition group at such a point, which is where it is cited.
